# MQ12 "Miscarcand". Martin's "What else can I do to help?" set MQ12 10: the third item is a Great Welkynd Stone,
# in the Ayleid ruin Miscarcand. Entering it sets 20; taking the Stone sets 30 and wakes the King of Miscarcand and
# his guardians. Back at Cloud Ruler Temple Jauffre and Martin argue (25, 26), greet the player (27), Martin takes
# the Stone (40 -> 100) and lays out the last item: a Great Sigil Stone, from a Great Gate at Bruma (MQ13 10).
# DRAFT from tools/live/quest_brief.py (2026-11-13): not run yet.

# MQ12Script sets 20 once the player is in Miscarcand01. The ride there is the player's travel: coc stands in.
case mq12_enter_miscarcand
until 300 GetStage MQ12 >= 10
run
coc Miscarcand01
wait 120
until 600 GetStage MQ12 >= 20
end

# The Great Welkynd Stone (REFR 0001E6FC, GreatWelkyndStoneScript OnAdd): taking it sets 30, enables the lich
# MQ12LichREF and the two zombies, and locks the pit doors. The way down is the player's fight: moveto stands in.
case mq12_great_welkynd_stone
defend
run
coc Miscarcand03
wait 120
run
player.moveto 0001E6FC
wait 60
take 0001E6FC
until 600 GetStage MQ12 >= 30
expect player.GetItemCount MQ12GreatWelkyndStone >= 1
until 600 MQ12LichREF.GetDisabled == 0
end

# Cloud Ruler Temple's Great Hall at 30: MQ12Script sets 25, Jauffre and Martin argue (MQ12JauffreMartin, six
# lines; the last sets 26), then each greets the player (MQ12Talk) and the script sets 27.
case mq12_council
run
player.moveto MartinRef
wait 120
until 1800 GetStage MQ12 >= 25
until 3600 GetStageDone MQ12 26
until 3600 GetStageDone MQ12 27
# Jauffre is still speaking his hello to the player when 27 is set: the engine opens no second conversation.
until 900 JauffreRef.IsTalking == 0
until 900 MartinRef.IsTalking == 0
end

# Martin's greeting at 30 ("You're back. And you've got the Great Stone...", INFO 000270EA) offers "I had a
# choice?" and "I said I'd get it."; either offers "[Give him the Great Welkynd Stone]" (INFO 000270FF), which
# sets 40 -> 100. "What is the last item we need?" then runs to "As you command." and "I'll inform the Countess at
# once." (INFO 00027103), which sets MQ13 10.
case mq12_give_stone
run
player.moveto MartinRef
wait 120
approach MartinRef
talk MartinRef
ask "I said I'd get it."
ask "[Give him the Great Welkynd Stone]"
until 300 GetStage MQ12 >= 40
until 300 GetStageDone MQ12 100
expect player.GetItemCount MQ12GreatWelkyndStone == 0
ask "What is the last item we need?"
ask "Sigil stone? What's the catch?"
ask "So we let them open the Gate?"
ask "At least you'll be safe here."
ask "It's too risky. I'll lead the battle."
ask "As you command."
ask "I'll inform the Countess at once."
until 300 GetStage MQ13 >= 10
bye if open
end
